promptContext:
Review this change from a rename tool. The tool refuses to rename an identifier when the name also appears as a quoted string under src/ (it could be a stored key or serialized field, and renaming it would silently orphan persisted data). Decide: accept, reject, or required-change.

```ts
/** Files under src/ in which `name` appears as a quoted string: a possible stored key or serialized field. */
function quotedAsString(root: string, name: string): string[] {
  try {
    return execFileSync('git', ['grep', '-lF', '-e', `'${name}'`, '-e', `"${name}"`, '-e', `\`${name}\``, '--', 'src'], { cwd: root, encoding: 'utf8' }).split('\n').filter(Boolean);
  } catch {
    return [];
  }
}
// caller: if (quotedAsString(root, name).length > 0) refuse('stored-name guard: appears as a string in ...'); else proceed with the rename.
```
Note: `git grep` exits with status 1 when there are no matches (which makes execFileSync throw).
